--TEST--
`Core\WebPush::subscription` accepts the `tainted` text a browser sent, and `Core\WebPush\Subscription::endpoint` returns `tainted string`, so a plain `string` return type does not accept it — `rule:core-classes/web-push-sends-an-encrypted-message` and `rule:security/tainted-qualifier`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\WebPush\Subscription::endpoint
// The browser wrote the endpoint. Nothing has checked where it points, so it stays `tainted`.
final class Push {
    public static function endpointOf(tainted string $json): string {
        return Core\WebPush::subscription($json)->endpoint();
    }
}
echo "unreachable\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0403]: this method declares `string` but returns `tainted string`
  --> case.nvs:6:16
